{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0edf5e8ace2f01205b327aa8b3d78fcc88f576721201043a63721ea1ad96b9ae"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documentation states file edits follow a review-before-write flow with path and command permission checks."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1d421d22562b7bb527ea10cec246578cb8fff75827e6a436c6038e20690e5f91"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documented slash commands include /plan for an in-memory Todo list, /goal with pause/resume for a Goal that persists across turns, and /loop for a recurring prompt with a default ten-minute interval and a one-minute minimum."},{"claim_ids":["clm_422237ee93d4c0d224dcf35b07e48b67a517cfe6a4a33c9c14e4e742a512c375"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documented local skills are discovered through SKILL.md files, alongside MCP tools, resources, and prompts reachable over stdio or remote HTTP."},{"claim_ids":["clm_49627410332c511d185a16e477eecb60833204ead2a36933c7761350a2d2e518"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documented core capabilities include multi-step tool execution within a single turn, forming a model-to-tool-to-model loop."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4dec81d428bee0b11483dff8f673d5685c95e7f99a88428e2a3381ca91cdc979"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The documented installer asks for a model name plus ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL and ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN, storing configuration under a dedicated home directory that can be relocated with the MINI_CODE_HOME variable."},{"claim_ids":["clm_746138e03329d7aaf8438de9d29b59a80e2f4c46a2a41af5401b95ad04f025be"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README describes MiniCode as a lightweight terminal coding assistant for local development, offering Claude Code-like workflow and architectural ideas in a much smaller implementation aimed at learning, experimentation, and custom tooling."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fef0f9b8cbeaeb0ae6dac1162487b8615c3878a13255360894637978ab0ad2be"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: Documented development commands are npm run check and npm test, alongside a stated goal of keeping the architecture understandable, hackable, and easy to extend."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0edf5e8ace2f01205b327aa8b3d78fcc88f576721201043a63721ea1ad96b9ae","clm_1d421d22562b7bb527ea10cec246578cb8fff75827e6a436c6038e20690e5f91","clm_422237ee93d4c0d224dcf35b07e48b67a517cfe6a4a33c9c14e4e742a512c375","clm_49627410332c511d185a16e477eecb60833204ead2a36933c7761350a2d2e518","clm_4dec81d428bee0b11483dff8f673d5685c95e7f99a88428e2a3381ca91cdc979","clm_746138e03329d7aaf8438de9d29b59a80e2f4c46a2a41af5401b95ad04f025be","clm_fef0f9b8cbeaeb0ae6dac1162487b8615c3878a13255360894637978ab0ad2be"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:48:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_91bb3d96df354a6396727bdaa47d32e8","id":"pg_436e670740ca515287590e04ea3efe33","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/liumengxuan04-minicode-readme-md-40413758cc12-0e04ea3efe33.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_ce4aa2ed2a995be3a9b644207b7d6a9c"],"title":"LiuMengxuan04/MiniCode/README.md @ 40413758cc12","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:48:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_91bb3d96df354a6396727bdaa47d32e8"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_114825a60fc34c1d8d312ca1f7f56dce379c14b0e1f7b1c7460e98bae80d9baa"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documentation lists planned-but-not-built items including full Ink/React rendering, bridge/IDE two-way communication, remote sessions, LSP support, and a skill marketplace, while noting a minimal sub-agent runtime and basic layered memory loading are already implemented."},{"claim_ids":["clm_40dc4f5aef9806c88552096ddcb9375b567853316f3303e9b0a1ef977b11fcd0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documentation states very large tool outputs are moved out of the prompt context and stored on disk, leaving the model a preview and a path to the full output."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4c019ef5a773046599f77e39a45913620653c5c44c0177de1818ae771b0fea28"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documented runtime state keeps conversation messages in memory during a turn, appends them to a per-project session log after each successful turn, and treats fresh provider-reported usage as the source of truth for context accounting, with local token estimation only as a fallback or a tail estimate."},{"claim_ids":["clm_72f5babcd14862814804547e09713d8b4dd2fab801551c1bcc46938470d0bbc5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documentation describes a root agent that can spawn up to three concurrent read-only sub-agents restricted to file search/read, skill loading, and web research tools; sub-agents cannot edit files, run commands, ask the user, or spawn further agents, and the root owns every code change."},{"claim_ids":["clm_dca464b68ac577dbf8fb71231ce1326e3f24725f39a523ad159ca7bb687f524c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documentation states this multi-agent MVP does not persist workers, load .claude/agents, support nesting, isolate worktrees, or allow live user steering, framing itself as a minimal teaching implementation."}],"claim_ids":["clm_114825a60fc34c1d8d312ca1f7f56dce379c14b0e1f7b1c7460e98bae80d9baa","clm_40dc4f5aef9806c88552096ddcb9375b567